# The optional hosted speech and embedding providers (Scott decisions 75 and 90). Copy this
# file to hosted-keys.env beside compose.yaml (mode 600), then uncomment and fill in only
# the lines you use; the repository never holds a real hosted-keys.env. Only the worker
# reads it, and without it the worker gets none of these variables. Every line here is
# commented out on purpose: copied as it is, the file sets nothing.
#
# A BASE_URL must be https:// when its key is set (the worker refuses to start otherwise).
# Values are read as in .env: a `$` in a value must be written `$$`. Keys never go into
# the database or the repository, and a preview refuses them.
#
# Rolling back to a build older than these settings (any build before commit 3f678e79):
# remove this file first, or that build's worker refuses the unknown variables and does
# not start.

# Hosted speech (P4-03): an OpenAI-compatible /v1/audio/speech API, used only for
# workspaces that allow hosted speech and never for a local-only project. On only when the
# URL, the model and the key are all set; the voice is optional.
# SPEECH__HOSTED_BASE_URL=
# SPEECH__HOSTED_MODEL=
# SPEECH__HOSTED_VOICE=
# SPEECH__HOSTED_API_KEY=

# Hosted embedder (P3-10): an OpenAI-compatible /v1/embeddings API. A local embedder, when
# configured, stays preferred, and a local-only project's text never goes here. On only
# when the URL, the model and the key are all set; DIMS is the model's vector size (blank:
# 1024, at most 2000).
# EMBEDDINGS__HOSTED_BASE_URL=
# EMBEDDINGS__HOSTED_MODEL=
# EMBEDDINGS__HOSTED_DIMS=
# EMBEDDINGS__HOSTED_API_KEY=
